From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kodi-iris contributors <kodi-iris@invalid>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:34:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] v4l2_m2m_dec: fail promptly when capture cannot restart
 after source change

Symptom: hevc_v4l2m2m on a 10-bit HEVC stream (which iris_driver
reports as NV12 at source change, then refuses with REQBUFS EBUSY) took
~12 s to fail: four 3 s capture poll timeouts ending in "A decoder
returned an unexpected error code" (ffmpeg exit 190). With -v debug the
same failure could even end as a silent EOF with 0 frames and exit 0.

do_source_change() ignored the result of the capture STREAMON (which
also covers buffer allocation), returned "reinit OK" and left the
decoder polling a capture queue with no buffers. Return the error so
get_qbuf() marks capture done and reports it, and stop the receive_frame
loop on a hard dequeue error instead of looping into the done capture
context, which turned the error into a plain EOF.

Verified: hevc10 now fails in ~70 ms with EINVAL (ffmpeg exit 69;
avcodec API consumer gets AVERROR(EINVAL)). tests/run-matrix.sh: all
27 cases PASS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 libavcodec/v4l2_context.c | 7 +++++++
 libavcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec.c | 7 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/v4l2_context.c b/libavcodec/v4l2_context.c
index 8be37aafed..52bd399a7a 100644
--- a/libavcodec/v4l2_context.c
+++ b/libavcodec/v4l2_context.c
@@ -387,6 +387,13 @@ static int do_source_change(V4L2m2mContext * const s)
     }
 
     ret = ff_v4l2_context_set_status(&s->capture, VIDIOC_STREAMON);
+    if (ret) {
+        // Without a running capture Q nothing more will ever be decoded
+        // (e.g. the driver refused to allocate buffers for this stream), so
+        // fail now rather than poll for frames that cannot arrive.
+        av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Source change: capture restart failed: %s\n", av_err2str(ret));
+        return ret;
+    }
     return 1;
 }
 
diff --git a/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec.c b/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec.c
index 1946166ced..23157f8308 100644
--- a/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec.c
@@ -687,9 +687,14 @@ static int v4l2_receive_frame(AVCodecContext *avctx, AVFrame *frame)
             else if (dst_rv == AVERROR_EOF && (s->draining || s->capture.done))
                 av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_DEBUG, "Dequeue EOF: draining=%d, cap.done=%d\n",
                        s->draining, s->capture.done);
-            else if (dst_rv && dst_rv != AVERROR(EAGAIN))
+            else if (dst_rv && dst_rv != AVERROR(EAGAIN)) {
                 av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Packet dequeue failure: draining=%d, cap.done=%d, err=%d\n",
                        s->draining, s->capture.done, dst_rv);
+                // Hard error: report it now. Looping would only find the
+                // capture context done and turn the error into a plain EOF.
+                if (dst_rv != AVERROR_EOF)
+                    break;
+            }
         }
 
         ++i;
